==Appearance==
Flyte is a tall butterfly, tall enough to be the tallest of all the [[Toons]]. He has pastel cyan skin and a head shaped like an upside-down teardrop or egg. Atop his head, he has two antennae that end in dark cyan clovers. He wears pink makeup under his eyelids and a long, dark cyan cloak which is the same color as his antennae. He sports pink fluff around his neck, and pastel pink wings with a sharp structure. Each wing has clover markings of a darker shade of pink on them on the upper halves. He has no visible arms or mouth. Flyte chooses to walk on foot instead of flying, but he can indeed fly, being much more obvious with {{CI|Twisted Flyte}}[[Twisted Flyte|his Twisted counterpart]], and eventually fully confirmed as of the music video for "[[Wilting]]" (as he is shown flying to grab a crate filled with eggs in one of the scenes).

==Personality==
Flyte is portrayed as an outgoing, caring, down to earth and friendly [[Toon]] who frequently checks up on the others to make sure they are okay. However, when some check up on him to see if he's okay or simply ask him certain questions, he tries to change the conversation. Much like a stereotypical older brother, he loves and cares deeply for his little sister {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}, but his worrying for her annoys her, and she gets frustrated whenever he tries to convince her to give her wings a break, which in turn leads to her teasing him for not using his own. The sibling-like bickering is practically at a very little amount, so they predominantly love and care about each other. Befitting his guardian-like nature, his protectiveness extends beyond his sister, as he actively looks out for Toons such as {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}} and {{CI|Rodger|name=true}}, trying to make sure that they don't get hurt.

The descriptions of some of his [[UGC Items]] state that he has a snarky attitude, but such a side of him has never been displayed anywhere (with the possible exception of him and his sister talking about how much he flies compared to her).

