===Golden Skin Strategies===
*'''For the first quest''', play normally until you see {{CI|Twisted Flyte|name=true}} on the [[Floor]]. Then, either encounter him normally or ask the distractor to bring Twisted Flyte to the Elevator. It is easier to do this when he's on the [[Daily Twisted Board]]. Additionally, you should only play until around Floors 5-10, as those are when {{Type|Uncommon}} Twisteds are the most common.
*'''For the second quest''', you should do a run with a good distractor or have friends that are willing to carry you. Once you reach Floor 21, you may leave if you want. Use survival Trinkets like {{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}} to help you, or use {{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}} to quicken Floor progression.
*'''For the third quest''', put down a gust and ask people to run through it. If you can't say that to them, make them do it subconsciously by putting it in useful spots like near the [[Elevator]] or next to the distractor.

==Strategies==
Flyte is an excellent All-Rounder [[Toon]] with 4{{Star}} [[Movement Speed]], 3 Star [[Stealth]], and 4 Star [[Extraction Speed]]. His [[Ability]], {{AI|Flyte|name=true}}, is quite beneficial, increasing Movement Speed for other Toons.

Flyte's 4 Star Movement Speed and 4 Star Extraction Speed means that he can distract and extract better than most other Toons. However, because these increases come at a cost of their other [[Stat]] counterpart (Stamina and Skill Check), there are still some things that get impeded. With 2 Star Stamina, escaping faster [[Twisteds]]/sprint tapping will be slightly harder to do as you lose around 2.5 seconds of Stamina that could be used by a 3 Star Stamina Toon. However, his 4 Star Movement Speed and Ability can make this slightly easier to deal with. On the extracting side, 2 Star Skill Check makes using common Skill Check [[Trinkets]] like {{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}} riskier due to the smaller size you have to hit. 4 Star Extraction Speed is fine, but if it repeatedly gets halted by Skill Check failures, it won't be as good. However, practicing small sizes or using other Trinkets like {{TI|Thinking Cap|name=true}} can help.

Though also generally useful, his Active Ability can come in handy for 1 Star Movement Speed Toons like {{CI|Connie|name=true}}, {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}}, and {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, since they may have trouble getting away from fast Twisteds like {{CI|Twisted Cocoa|name=true}} and {{CI|Twisted Shelly|name=true}}. In addition, the gust can affect himself, unlike other speed boosting Abilities that can only affect Toons other than the user; this is one of the biggest pros of Gust despite its relatively low potency.

Other applications for Flyte's Ability include:
*Escaping Twisteds, being able to be used like {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}'s {{AI|Flutter|name=true}} Ability;
*Using it in front of other Toons to both boost them and insert oneself in front of the Twisteds to take aggro. Positioning matters; try not to put your boost behind them;
*To grant a speed boost to teammates at the start of a Floor to give your distractor an early start and generally to get the most out of it;
*Helping others get to the [[Elevator]] in time, by putting it a decent distance away (so other Toons get the most use out of it) if possible. Pay attention to who's outside/approaching and time it when most of them are close, as the gust does disappear after a while. Therefore, try to save your Ability for [[Panic Mode]] once a majority of [[Machines]] have been completed;
*Boosting the distractor while they're dealing with dangerous scenarios. Try not to randomly boost them without warning; the speed may throw them off if they're not dealing with specific threats. Use your Ability on distractors at the beginning of Floors, near the Elevator during Panic Mode, when they're dealing with {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}}/{{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}}, and if they seem to be struggling or to take aggro from them if you're backup. Try not to "help" them otherwise unless they communicate differently. When boosting them, try to anticipate their path and put it there before they even get close so that you don't get in their way unless your Stealth is higher. This tactic can also be used if you are distracting.
*Placing the gust on a Treadmill Machine to make himself or another Toon more efficient at extracting them.
*Placing the gust under a Toon who is low on Stamina or ran out of Stamina, to allow them to safely walk faster while regenerating, though this requires good communication. This can also be applied to himself.
*Placing it in blackouts to light up the paths.

Flyte's Ability affects other Toons equally, acting as a physical "power-up" that others must touch to receive the buff. His Ability works on himself as well, making it easy to use during chases where multiple Toons are at risk. Note that a 15% Movement Speed boost for 3 seconds won't always be enough to escape Twisteds.

Flyte's gust during a [[Blackout]] can also produce light. While it's not much light, it can still help other players navigate through the Floors or make it easier for players to know where an [[Item]] could be like a {{II|Bandage|name=false}} or a {{II|Health Kit|name=false}} if they had a hard time trying to find the Item in the dark. Highlighting the Elevator or correct path during Panic Mode may be helpful for new players with low graphics settings.

During [[Ichor Leaks]], you could try to place the gust by Ichor Puddles in order to reduce the slowness applied by them. This can especially help if any puddles are in an important path, such as a distractor's looping area, a safe way back to the Elevator, and a healer's route to an injured Toon. Do note that this won’t fully neutralize or counter the slowness (Toons will still get -2% Movement Speed), but it can reduce it to a minor inconvenience.

Good Items to focus on are Movement Speed Items to allow Flyte to outwalk Twisteds temporarily with his 4 Star speed, or to stack with his Ability's boost. Stamina Items can help with the below average capacity, making things a bit safer especially as a distractor. Extraction related Items, particularly if they boost Extraction Speed like {{II|Instructions|name=false}} will help improve Flyte's above average extraction. 

Overall, he functions pretty similarly to other Toons with speed boosting support Abilities, just without certain traits like an effective counter to Ichor Leaks or a way to directly help with Stamina. He still has his own strengths and advantages, being a great Toon in solo runs.

