==Trivia==
*Flyte being {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}'s older brother makes them the fourth set of in-game [[Toons]] to have a canonical biological relationship.
*Flyte and Flutter share many similarities and contrasting points, both of which work together to unify their connection;
**Their names are ways of referring to a group of butterflies, and describing how they fly (a flutter and a flight).
**Their color palettes both involve the use of pink and turquoise.
***Flyte's color palette is the opposite of Flutter's, having a dominant blue and secondary pink compared to the reverse for Flutter.
**Their [[Twisted]] alternates never stop actively moving when roaming the map.
**Their body shapes and heights seem to add on to a duo trope where one member is short and plump, while the other is tall and lanky.
**They share the same [[Ability]] sound.
**Their Abilities involve spinning and boosting Movement Speed.
**Flyte's clover motifs seem to be carried over from old concept art of Flutter, with her having the same clover pattern on her wings as Flyte (albeit all over).
*As of v0.8.1, Flyte is the tallest [[Toon]] in the game, being even taller than {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} (the original tallest Toon prior to Flyte's introduction).
*Before the changes in the [[Changelog|v0.8.4]] Easter Patch, there used to be a bug where Flyte's {{AI|Flyte|name=true}} [[Ability]] will make any nearby [[Twisteds]] stop chasing him, along with preventing long-ranged Twisteds from using their abilities properly, due to his Ability acting like an obstacle where the Twisteds' line of sight is completely prevented, essentially turning him into a living [[Smoke Bomb]].
*Flyte has a model error in the form of a dent in the left side of his head. This is usually not visible in-game but can be seen in certain lighting.
*Flyte shares the same requirements as [[Ginger]] and [[Soulvester]]; 700 of the [[Event]]'s [[Currency]], and 50% [[Research]] on their own [[Twisted Flyte|Twisted]].
*Flyte is the fourth [[Toon]] in the game to be an actual living thing, rather than an object (a butterfly).
*Flyte's {{Skin|Luna Moth}} [[Skin]] is inspired by and named after the real-life {{wp|luna moth}} species. [[Flutter]]'s {{Skin|Rosy Maple Moth}} Skin follows the exact same logic, as the {{wp|rosy maple moth}} is also a real species. Alongside their Spring-Time Skins, this means they have two sets of matching Skins and not just one.
*The "Happy Easter!" video depicts what looks like Flyte standing upright while sleeping, but he also appears to simply lean with his back against the wall.<ref>[[File:Happy_Easter!🌷-_Dandy’s_World|200x200px]]</ref> Regardless of whatever he's truly doing, Flutter can most likely do the same thing.
*Despite being featured in the song [[Wilting]], Flyte and [[Eggson]] do not have any lines.
*Flyte's full render does not match his in-game model.
*His skins for the 2026 easter event all have a texture error that makes his face too big.

